Third-party data — not covered by the MIT licence above

The MIT licence covers the software in this repository: the build scripts, the
application in src/main.js and src/style.css, the tests and the configuration.

It does not and cannot cover the virological data, which is not the copyright
holder's to relicense:

  data-src/VMR_MSL41.v1.20260729.xlsx and everything derived from it in
  src/data/catalog.js — the ICTV Virus Metadata Resource, (c) International
  Committee on Taxonomy of Viruses, CC BY 4.0.
  https://ictv.global/vmr

  The mechanism values in scripts/curated/families.mjs, and the ViralZone page
  ids in data-src/ — derived from ViralZone, (c) SIB Swiss Institute of
  Bioinformatics, CC BY 4.0.
  https://viralzone.expasy.org

Both remain under CC BY 4.0. Reusing them, including by reusing this
repository, carries the attribution requirement with it.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The scope, confidence and note text written for this project is the copyright
holder's own and is offered under CC BY 4.0 on the same terms, so that a curated
row can be reused as a whole without untangling which clause came from where.
